        <briefdescription>
<para>Constructs a reference to a callable. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The callable must be invocable with a <computeroutput>Self_T&amp;</computeroutput> argument, and must outlive the reference.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Callable_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the callable object.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Constraints</title><para><computeroutput>Callable_T</computeroutput> is not a <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1callable__ref" kindref="compound">callable_ref</ref></computeroutput>, so that the copy constructor is used for copies.</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>callable</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The callable object; a non-<computeroutput>const</computeroutput> lvalue.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Stores the address of the callable, and the address of the <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1callable__ref_1affde2e2f927df6b5ada7f5578f8d5c36" kindref="member">invoke_callable()</ref></computeroutput> instantiation for its type. </para>
