        <briefdescription>
<para>Invokes a callable of a given type, from its address. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Instantiated by the constructor for the type of the callable; its address is stored in <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1callable__ref_1a7ca4453fe089a72345a476490212ae59" kindref="member">invoke_</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Callable_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the callable object.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>callable</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The address of the callable, with its type erased. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>self</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The reference passed to the callable. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Returns</title><para>Nothing.</para>
</simplesect>
Casts <computeroutput>callable</computeroutput> back to <computeroutput>Callable_T*</computeroutput>, the type it had when the reference was constructed, and invokes the callable through it, as an lvalue, with <computeroutput>self</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>A function pointer or a function object is called directly, not through <computeroutput>std::invoke()</computeroutput>, which, without optimisations, adds three frames to the call chain; a pointer to a member, which only <computeroutput>std::invoke()</computeroutput> can call, is still passed to it. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="/Users/ilg/MyProjects/micro-os-plus.github/xPacks/micro-test-plus-xpack.git/include/micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus/test.h" line="889" column="7" bodyfile="/Users/ilg/MyProjects/micro-os-plus.github/xPacks/micro-test-plus-xpack.git/include/micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus/inlines/test-inlines.h" bodystart="360" bodyend="370"/>
      </memberdef>
    </sectiondef>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Non-owning reference to a callable invoked with a <computeroutput>Self_T&amp;</computeroutput> argument. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Holds the address of the callable and a pointer to a function, instantiated for its type, which converts the address back and invokes the callable. Unlike a <computeroutput>std::function</computeroutput>, it neither copies the callable nor allocates memory, so the callable must outlive the reference.</para>
<para>A test case refers to its body this way, since the body is a local object of <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1runnable__base_1ad4ac49522cfd6e1608d9ac64ab7a8b91" kindref="member">runnable_base::create_test_case()</ref></computeroutput>, which runs the test case and destroys it before returning.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Self_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type referred to by the argument of the callable (<computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1test__case" kindref="compound">test_case</ref></computeroutput>). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
